## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to model non-crossing, higher-arity structures with DP and reconstruct a solution.

## Key Concepts

- DP state dp[i][t] for i and t
- Non-crossing triple formation
- Reconstruction via backpointers
- Time/space trade-offs and optimization path

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxTriples(A, n, k) {
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) {
        for (let i1=1; i1<i; i1++) {
          for (let j=i1+1; j<i; j++) {
            const prev = (i1>=2 ? dp[i1-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : -Infinity));
            const val = prev + A[i1-1]*A[j-1]*A[i-1];
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; prv[i][t] = {i1, j}; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction logic would backtrack using prv
  return {value: dp[n][k], triples: []};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests understanding of partition dynamic programming with nontrivial segment costs, requiring careful recurrence formulation, efficient range query handling, and solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with fixed number of contiguous segments
- Segment cost computation using range max-min queries
- Reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space optimization techniques

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartitions(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const pre = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  // Base case: single segment
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    let maxVal = A[0], minVal = A[0];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      maxVal = Math.max(maxVal, A[j]);
      minVal = Math.min(minVal, A[j]);
      dp[i][1] = maxVal - minVal;
    }
  }

  // DP transitions
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const segmentCost = computeCost(A, j + 1, i);
        if (dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost;
          pre[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = pre[end][t] + 1;
    segments.unshift([start, end]);
    end = pre[end][t];
  }

  return { minCost: dp[n][k], segments };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with subarray composition where each block incurs a fixed cost, a realistic pattern in scheduling/payments. It also checks reconstruction of intervals.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums to compute subarray sums fast
- DP over positions and block counts
- Optimization: collapse inner max with a running best value per t
- Backpointer reconstruction for endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraySumMinusC(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const endAt = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = Array(k+1).fill(-1e15);
  const bestIdx = Array(k+1).fill(-1);
  bestVal[1] = 0; bestIdx[1] = 1; // allow start at 1 for first block
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      const endVal = pref[i] - c + bestVal[t];
      if (dp[i-1][t] >= endVal) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      } else {
        dp[i][t] = endVal;
        endAt[i][t] = {start: bestIdx[t], end: i};
      }
    }
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      const cand = dp[i][t-1] - pref[i];
      if (cand > bestVal[t]) { bestVal[t] = cand; bestIdx[t] = i+1; }
    }
  }
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const e = endAt[i][t];
    if (e) { blocks.push([e.start, e.end]); i = e.start - 1; t--; }
    else { i--; }
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

